  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="support-faq section-light">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item" id="flux-demo">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can I try the Flux app without Home Assistant?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. On the Flux connection screen, tap <strong>Try the Demo</strong> to explore the entire app with realistic sample data &mdash; dashboards, controls, automations, and animated artwork &mdash; with no Home Assistant server or account required.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item" id="flux-connect">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>How do I connect Flux to Home Assistant?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Open Flux and enter your Home Assistant address (for example <code>homeassistant.local:8123</code> or your Home Assistant Cloud / Nabu Casa URL) plus a Long-Lived Access Token. Create a token in Home Assistant under your profile &rarr; Security &rarr; Long-Lived Access Tokens, then tap Connect. Flux works over your local network or remotely.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item" id="flux-troubleshoot">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Flux won't connect &mdash; what should I check?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Make sure your device and Home Assistant are on the same network (for local connections), the address includes the correct port (usually 8123), and your access token is valid and hasn't been revoked. For remote access, confirm Home Assistant Cloud (Nabu Casa) or your reverse proxy is reachable. Your URL and token are stored securely in the iOS Keychain and survive app updates.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Are my Flux dashboards synced, and is my data private?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>If you enable iCloud for Flux, your dashboards sync privately across your iPhone, iPad, and Apple TV through your own iCloud account. Flux connects directly to your Home Assistant &mdash; there is no Flux cloud, no account, and no analytics or tracking. See our <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Do I need Home Assistant to use Flux products?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Our products are designed to work with Home Assistant. The Irrigation Controller, Gophr Probe, and TPH Sensor all use ESPHome firmware and integrate seamlessly with your Home Assistant setup. The Night Light can also be flashed with WLED as an alternative firmware.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can I 3D print the Night Light housing?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes! We provide STL files for the Night Light housing. You can buy just the circuit board from our store and print the housing yourself. The files are optimized for FDM printers and require no supports.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>How many zones does the Irrigation Controller support?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>The base unit supports 8 zones. With expansion boards (MCP23017 I2C), you can expand up to 32 zones total. Zone 8 can also be configured as a master valve or pump start relay.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>What protocols does the Gophr probe support?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Gophr supports three protocol options: ESPHome (WiFi, our primary recommendation), Zigbee (for mesh networks and extended range), and Matter (for broad smart home platform compatibility). Choose the variant that fits your setup when purchasing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Is the Management Dashboard required?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Absolutely not. The management dashboard is entirely optional. All Flux products work independently with Home Assistant. The dashboard is a convenience layer for professionals who manage multiple properties &mdash; it does not gate any hardware functionality.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>How do firmware updates work?</span>
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="faq-chevron"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>All Flux devices support OTA (Over-the-Air) updates. When connected to Home Assistant, updates can be pushed from the ESPHome dashboard. The Night Light also has a built-in web server for direct browser-based updates, and GitHub-hosted firmware releases.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

